spec sk04-cross-label-write-skew: 2 sessions, 20 permutations
# SK04. Rule: a project's manager must be a manager. s1 checks that person p is a
# manager and creates a project managed by p; s2 checks that no project names p and
# demotes p. They read and write different labels, so both commit where their reads
# precede each other's commits: SI permits the broken rule.

starting permutation: s1r s1w s1c s2r s2w s2c
step s1r: MATCH (p:Person {name:'p'}) RETURN p.manager AS manager
manager
-------
true   
(1 row)
step s1w: CREATE (j:Project {name:'proj', manager:'p'}) RETURN j.name AS project
project
-------
"proj" 
(1 row)
step s1c: COMMIT
step s2r: MATCH (j:Project {manager:'p'}) RETURN count(j) AS projects
projects
--------
0       
(1 row)
step s2w: MATCH (p:Person {name:'p'}) SET p.manager = false RETURN p.manager AS manager
manager
-------
false  
(1 row)
step s2c: COMMIT
final final: MATCH (p:Person {name:'p'}) OPTIONAL MATCH (j:Project {manager:'p'}) RETURN p.manager AS manager, count(j) AS projects
manager|projects
-------+--------
false  |1       
(1 row)

